<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Shrinivasa Malla</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">17th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Shrinivasa Malla was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitpur">Lalitpur</a> (Patan) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a> in the second half of the 17th century. The son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/siddhi-narasimha-malla">Siddhi Narasimha Malla</a>, he added buildings to the royal palace complex on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/patan-durbar-square">Patan Durbar Square</a> and restored temples. His reign was marked by shifting alliances and wars with the rival Malla kingdoms of Kantipur and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bhaktapur">Bhaktapur</a>.</p></div>
